        <paragraph>The object enters along a path approximated by the line $$y = 2x - 2$$ and passes within 0.5 au of the sun at its closest approach, so the sun is one focus of the hyperbola. It then departs the solar system along a path approximated by the line $$y = -2x + 2.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$4(x-1)2-y22=16 4(x-1)2-y22=16$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="68" has_solution="false">
